                        "tags": [
                            "positive",
                            "predicative",
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "sie sind unüberschreitbar"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7a3122ad-140b-3e16-b0fc-026196cab799",
                        "entry_id": "6f75fb5b-f080-3f41-89e2-100334376107",
                        "glosses": [
                            "so, dass es nicht überschritten werden kann"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figurative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a5c65c4-2c0e-40a2-aa6c-2b2529c600fe",
                                "sense_id": "7a3122ad-140b-3e16-b0fc-026196cab799",
                                "text": "„Diese Grenze ist freilich unüberschreitbar, denn mit ihrer Aufhebung verflüchtigte sich die Natur; aber innerhalb ihrer ist nichts ihm prinzipiell unmöglich, und innerhalb ihrer liegt die Welt.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "73dec5a1-bc6c-4818-9ff8-95adbc616155",
                                "sense_id": "7a3122ad-140b-3e16-b0fc-026196cab799",
                                "text": "„Hier zuerst und zuletzt stand unüberschreitbar die große Grenze zwischen der Kraft und der Gnade, zwischen Tat und Leiden, zwischen Mensch und Gott.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2bb3a077-7d93-41d9-bf37-490702025d51",
                                "sense_id": "7a3122ad-140b-3e16-b0fc-026196cab799",
                                "text": "„In einer schutzlosen Welt ist ein Geisterschutz errichtet, der unüberschreitbar, unzerstörbar ist. »Ihr seid Götter« sagt einmal bedeutsam die Bibel. Diese Wahrheit ist unerschütterlich, aber auch unerschöpflich.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a2e9e495-4de1-4030-98db-ed6f3abc2d85",
                        "source_entry_id": "6f75fb5b-f080-3f41-89e2-100334376107",
                        "source_sense_id": "7a3122ad-140b-3e16-b0fc-026196cab799",
                        "source_sense_description": "auch übertragen: so, dass es nicht überschritten werden kann",
                        "target_lang_word": "impassable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "impassable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9d1e6460-73a0-391a-8c3b-de09fa13c566",
                                        "entry_id": "72e7d697-1410-3bd1-b4ab-7bc3e8e16bcb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Incapable of being passed over, crossed, or negotiated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8aa6f0cd-27fa-4b28-a2ac-59f4522adeae",
                                                "sense_id": "9d1e6460-73a0-391a-8c3b-de09fa13c566",
                                                "text": "At the same time, the encroachment of vegetation proceeds apace, and broom and brambles have already made portions of the line impassable, even on foot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06ecef8a-c61d-4335-8934-bbd042b6dba2",
                                                "sense_id": "9d1e6460-73a0-391a-8c3b-de09fa13c566",
                                                "text": "[...] at Cowley Bridge Junction, east of Exeter, both lines were impassable from about 1.30 p.m.—the first flooding of the junction for 36 years—and by the evening the water had risen two-thirds of the way up the platforms at St. Davids as Exeter faced its worst flooding for 60 years."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e1f8d17e-ee5c-3f13-8c48-853b9dbc35ff",
                                        "entry_id": "72e7d697-1410-3bd1-b4ab-7bc3e8e16bcb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Incapable of being overcome or surmounted."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of an obstacle"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc656ceb-7e3a-3086-a286-77cde86d2627",
                                        "entry_id": "72e7d697-1410-3bd1-b4ab-7bc3e8e16bcb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not usable as legal tender."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of currency"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8feb420e-4554-4397-8e5f-776d034187b1",
                        "source_entry_id": "6f75fb5b-f080-3f41-89e2-100334376107",
                        "source_sense_id": "7a3122ad-140b-3e16-b0fc-026196cab799",
                        "source_sense_description": "auch übertragen: so, dass es nicht überschritten werden kann",
                        "target_lang_word": "uncrossable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "uncrossable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "483042d9-c56d-3700-aa0a-de062916c28d",
                                        "entry_id": "b7bcca42-fa26-35da-b70f-2f94c6420ce1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Impossible to cross."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ad59013-fe75-49e1-841e-478ae350575b",
                                                "sense_id": "483042d9-c56d-3700-aa0a-de062916c28d",
                                                "text": "There is what appears under normal circumstances to be an uncrossable boundary, a total barrier."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94a9b954-e03c-4e8a-9a07-e5f9b90dd5b9",
                                                "sense_id": "483042d9-c56d-3700-aa0a-de062916c28d",
                                                "text": "And it’s brilliantly stitched together by motifs of chrysalises and movies and by a joyous abundance of metaphor and simile: “the ding of a bicycle bell like struck crystal”; a woman “talking for much of the day in a steady soft uncrossable stream.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db462961-1a57-4c08-9ecb-5a44bd3cc025",
                                                "sense_id": "483042d9-c56d-3700-aa0a-de062916c28d",
                                                "text": "There are very few bridges on the footpaths in Skye and even short periods of heavy rain can cause rivers to rise rapidly, often making them uncrossable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c55a2443-c18c-4302-b8f6-f2fd311fc3b1",
                                                "sense_id": "483042d9-c56d-3700-aa0a-de062916c28d",
                                                "text": "There are two Underground stations. That serving the District and Piccadilly is on one side of an uncrossable road called Hammersmith Broadway; that serving the Hammersmith & City is on the other side. Whichever exit you emerge from, at whichever station, you are immediately lost."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
